MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=7
DESCRIPTION=File history for server file sharing. Every share now keeps an append-only history in the host catalog (table catalog_event, same database as the share, one row per event with a per-share sequence number): offered when the sender registers it, completed with the content hash when the bytes land, accepted (with the disposition, overwrite, server-share or keep), declined, revoked by the owner, and expired when the host purges it. Events are written from the same code paths that change the share, so a change and its record cannot disagree, and a re-share no longer loses the earlier hash, because the offer's placeholder is replaced once and the history keeps it. The new shell verb server file history <share_id> prints a share's events in order. The catalog contract gains fl_server_catalog_append_event and fl_server_catalog_list_events (contracts/storage/contract_p5_server_catalog.h). Tests: new make test_file_history (offer, completion, expiry and sequence order per share) in run_all_tests.sh; test_server_shared_catalog and the accept path test still pass. Co-signed files: a newer copy of a file the recipient holds is refused unless the editor's supervisor has countersigned that revision (the scope owner or an ancestor, over the author's verified signature), with the new code NEEDS_EDITOR_PERMIT and the copy held kept. The supervisor adds the permit with server file permit <path>; a permitted revision goes out with server file send -t <path> -user <name> --permitted, which seals the head without a new check-in. The file's own history is read offline with server file log <path> (no session, no host), with names for each event code. KeyQuorum (ffi/identity) gains kq_file_events, kq_file_permits_newer and kq_file_countersign, and a check-in made through the FFI now records the same events as the CLI. Tests: test_kq_checkpoint covers the refusal, the permitted path, the offline history and the names. The browser lab has the same commands (server file permit <tracked copy>, server file log <path>, and send -t --permitted), but no history panel. Not covered yet: a panel in the lab, and the lab's WebAssembly build was not rebuilt here.

RELEASE_DATE=2026-10-21
